# Chicago citation helper

When editing or creating files under `06-references/`:

1. Use **Chicago notes-bibliography** (not author-date), unless the assessment brief specifies otherwise.
2. Bibliography entries: hanging-indent style described in plain Markdown (indent continuation lines with two spaces if useful).
3. Order alphabetically by first author’s surname; works with no author go under title.
4. Include DOI as URL when available (`https://doi.org/...`).
5. For web sources, include access date when no publication date is clear.
6. Never invent bibliographic data. List **Missing details to verify** for gaps.
7. Follow examples in `templates/chicago-reference.md`.
